    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Oh, definitely, definitely just thin gold line family. I have 911, just all of it. And it's so good to have you back. But I want to jump in here really quick. We've only got so much time. I want to jump in because one of the things that we want to get some clarification from is this Consolidated Appropriations Act. So we had done a dispatcher's round table a few weeks ago where we were talking about the 911 Saves Act and so many other things. There's a portion in a press release. And it says AIDS 911 operator. So the first portion here says directs the Office of Management and Budget to reclassify public safety telecommunicators by the end of fiscal year 23. Now there's a grant program as well that we're going to talk about here in just a moment about the funding. But that little piece, what exactly does that mean?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
